      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "KEITH BOWLES, : Petitioner"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court document",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "HARRY RUSSELL, WARDEN :"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court document",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Monday, March 26, 2007"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court document",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0000-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MALCOLM L. STEWART, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Mancino, your position here is that this rule is not jurisdictional. Now, what -- what are the consequences of that? I take it that that would mean that the court of appeals has no obligation to inquire on its own whether the matter has been filed too late?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. MANCINO",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MANCINO: No, I do not. We're relying to the exceptions, and there's a number exceptions on deadlines that have come out. We have the equitable tolling, we have the waiver, forfeiture issue. And, you know, in this case, specific assurance by a court which in a past opinion seemed to control the date, where a judge gave you a specific assurance that you could do something in connection with the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0001-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So this, obviously the motion to reopen was timely filed, was filed within the 180 days required by the rule. The other side was served. The other side had no objection to it and didn't oppose it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What type of jurisdiction are you speaking of? It's certainly not Federal jurisdiction in the sense of subject matter jurisdiction, like a specific case arising under Federal law. What kind of jurisdiction do you have in mind?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Number one, it can't be waived, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiff's Counsel",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "PLAINTIFF'S COUNSEL: No, Your Honor. The\ncase that they're citing to is Thompson, and in Thompson\nwhat occurred in that case is that the litigant in that\ncase --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "THE COURT: We'll hear from Mr. Stewart."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Paul Mancino, Jr.)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MANCINO: If this were a case where\nsomeone just missed the 30-day deadline, I don't think\nwe would be talking. We are talking about a case where\na judge properly found, properly ruled that notice was\nnot given and had the authority to reopen the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What would you, what would you have had to have done to find out when it was entered on the docket? Could you have accessed that electronically? Or would you have to go to the court, to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-5306",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fa5493e9c2c488a7d84ad519f3b25222729a0d5899c9288b44086c54fe8299ec",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fa5493e9c2c4-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Mr. Mancino. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, the case in the above-titled matter was submitted at 12:07 p.m.)"
    },
